  "description": "Boss's input buffer: an emitter follower (Q1) biased at half the supply through R2, so the guitar sees about 470k, and a low-impedance output after C2. R1 and C1 on the way in. Values and refs from ElectroSmash's \"Boss DS-1 Distortion Analysis\" (electrosmash.com/boss-ds1-analysis), as the DS-1 starter, with our own 2SC2240 card. The DS-1 uses the same follower as its output buffer. Biased from a reference voltage (vref port: wire it to a Vref divider).",
